      "review_date": "2015-10-01",
      "review_date_formatted": "",
      "overall_rating": 0,
      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "I had two quotes done and both salesmen stated that I needed a 5KW system which I was more than happy to have and wanted, but I had previously received a letter from Western Power stating I could only install a system up to 3KW, due to the size of the electrical cable (10mm) and the lead in distance from the green dome on the boundary of my property to my meter box (some 22 meters), although the Solargain salesman's graph indicated other wise, very frustrating. This was after receiving a letter from my electricity retailer thanking me as I was helping the environment by installing the system! Surely installing a 5KW system would help even more!!So my suggestion is directed to those people building a new house and are contemplating installing a solar system; ensure your builder installs an electrical cable big enough to service the solar system you desire.Also, I went with Solargain as the salesman sold the system on its merit and did not bag other resellers or systems, unlike the other salesman. And by the way, the other salesman under cut Solargain by $500 and stated he would install the inverter Solargain was supplying but would not install the same panels. It just came down to \"Trust\" in the end. When will these type of companies and salesmen learn (not just in the solar system industry)!",
